From 9051742a122ca2a8a5fca2efaa201ede8d4a13d2
Subject: web-worker: RenderCapabilities resource for main-world capability checks
Origin: https://github.com/robtfm/bevy/commit/9051742a122ca2a8a5fca2efaa201ede8d4a13d2
Date: 2026-09-18T23:54:15+01:00

Main-world code that only needs limits, features or adapter info (cluster
assignment, the skin uniform-buffer check, compressed-format detection in the
image and glTF loaders) now reads a RenderCapabilities resource. Normally it
wraps and derefs to the RenderDevice; with the web-worker feature it is a
snapshot taken on the render worker at finish, and the wgpu handles are no
longer inserted into the main world at all, so nothing there can touch them
across threads. The existing (&RenderDevice, &RenderAdapter) helpers keep
their signatures and delegate to `_with(&RenderCapabilities)` cores.
---
